WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.466 --> 00:00:01.531
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.531 --> 00:00:04.059
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe,

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:05.564
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.564 --> 00:00:07.756
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:09.398
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:09.398 --> 00:00:12.818
today's message is stop believing in luck.

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:15.068
Over to you, Oprah Winfrey.

00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:19.728
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.467
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.967
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:30.964
- Nothing about my life is lucky, nothing.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.662
A lot of grace, a lot of blessings,

00:00:35.662 --> 00:00:39.829
a lot of divine order, but
I don't believe in luck.

00:00:41.103 --> 00:00:43.606
For me luck is preparation

00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:46.439
meeting the moment of opportunity.

00:00:47.785 --> 00:00:51.952
There is no luck without
you being prepared

00:00:51.952 --> 00:00:55.103
to handle that moment of opportunity,

00:00:55.103 --> 00:00:57.115
and so what I would say for myself

00:00:57.115 --> 00:01:00.115
is that because of my hand in a hand

00:01:00.951 --> 00:01:03.616
and a force greater than my own,

00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:05.884
I have been prepared in ways

00:01:05.884 --> 00:01:09.297
that I didn't even know
I was being prepared for,

00:01:09.297 --> 00:01:13.130
and the truth is, for
me and for every person,

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:19.341
every single thing that has
ever happened in your life

00:01:19.341 --> 00:01:23.341
is preparing you for the
moment that is to come.

00:01:24.798 --> 00:01:26.996
- So I'm not a huge
believer in luck either.

00:01:26.996 --> 00:01:29.499
You know, was it lucky
that I was born in Canada?

00:01:29.499 --> 00:01:30.501
Yes.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.140
Was it lucky that I have amazing parents?

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.150
Yes.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.025
Was it lucky that I
didn't get hit by a bus

00:01:35.025 --> 00:01:37.753
on the way to the studio
today to film for you guys?

00:01:37.753 --> 00:01:38.753
Yes.

00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:42.471
Was it lucky for me in entrepreneurship?

00:01:42.471 --> 00:01:44.877
Did it help in my business career?

00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:45.710
Maybe.

00:01:46.587 --> 00:01:49.256
What I love doing is looking at success.

00:01:49.256 --> 00:01:50.513
I love modeling success,

00:01:50.513 --> 00:01:52.631
and I look at who's had the most success,

00:01:52.631 --> 00:01:54.613
who are the people who
built the big companies,

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:57.005
and it's almost never the people

00:01:57.005 --> 00:02:01.625
who are the children of
really wealthy people.

00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:05.154
It's almost never the people
who have the most luck

00:02:05.154 --> 00:02:09.414
in the world, who had everything
kind of handed to them.

00:02:09.414 --> 00:02:13.261
They had the most opportunity
to create amazing things.

00:02:13.261 --> 00:02:15.794
They had connections and they
had money and they had family

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:18.415
and they had relationships
and they had education,

00:02:18.415 --> 00:02:22.556
all the things that people
think are really important.

00:02:22.556 --> 00:02:26.024
Look at the top people who
built the most amazing companies

00:02:26.024 --> 00:02:29.333
and look at their backgrounds.

00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:32.297
Most of them started off with nothing.

00:02:32.297 --> 00:02:35.032
Most of them don't credit education,

00:02:35.032 --> 00:02:37.639
a formal education at
least as being a thing

00:02:37.639 --> 00:02:41.172
that really helped them, if
they even had formal education.

00:02:41.172 --> 00:02:43.375
Most of them didn't have
great family connections.

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:44.970
A lot of them are immigrants

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.705
who came to the country with zero.

00:02:46.705 --> 00:02:48.018
The ones who were born here

00:02:48.018 --> 00:02:49.487
didn't have a lot of money either.

00:02:49.487 --> 00:02:53.003
Despite them being unlucky,
these are the guys who made it,

00:02:53.003 --> 00:02:55.202
and so I think a lot of people blame luck

00:02:55.202 --> 00:02:58.223
for them not having success.

00:02:58.223 --> 00:03:00.214
You look at someone
who's had massive success

00:03:00.214 --> 00:03:02.891
and say, "Well, they were
just lucky," and you know why?

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:04.901
'Cause it makes you feel
good about yourself.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:08.210
'Cause as long as you can
believe that it's luck

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.162
that is causing these
people to be successful,

00:03:11.162 --> 00:03:12.871
it's luck that he got that loan

00:03:12.871 --> 00:03:16.017
or luck that she built
that business or luck,

00:03:16.017 --> 00:03:17.680
as long as you believe it's luck,

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.738
then you don't have to take
any personal responsibility.

00:03:21.738 --> 00:03:22.734
You're just not lucky.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:23.727
That's not your fault.

00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:25.041
It's not your fault you're not lucky.

00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:26.630
Those guys are lucky, you're not lucky.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.532
You're the same as them,
you worked just as hard,

00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:29.972
you have the greatest
ideas just like them.

00:03:29.972 --> 00:03:31.161
The only difference is luck.

00:03:31.161 --> 00:03:32.789
And if that's what you believe,

00:03:32.789 --> 00:03:34.751
then you're going to stay
exactly where you are,

00:03:34.751 --> 00:03:36.263
and so that's the difference.

00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:39.205
Taking personal accountability and saying,

00:03:39.205 --> 00:03:41.748
"I am where I am because of me."

00:03:41.748 --> 00:03:44.591
Growing up, you know, you're
living with your parents,

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:48.087
you take on their values, you
do what they ask you to do

00:03:48.087 --> 00:03:50.641
to some extent, but at
some point you decide,

00:03:50.641 --> 00:03:52.747
"I'm an adult, I'm
going to change my life.

00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:54.695
"I'm going to set the course
for what I'm going to do."

00:03:54.695 --> 00:03:56.465
It's nobody else's fault anymore.

00:03:56.465 --> 00:03:58.656
You know, if you're not being fed

00:03:58.656 --> 00:04:01.118
when you're three years
old, that's not your fault.

00:04:01.118 --> 00:04:04.199
But if you're not being fed
when you're 25 years old,

00:04:04.199 --> 00:04:07.240
30 years old, 40 years
old, that's your fault.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.533
You got to get out and
start doing the work,

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.197
and so I think a lot of
people just blame bad luck

00:04:12.197 --> 00:04:15.427
as an excuse for not doing the work.

00:04:15.427 --> 00:04:16.969
I'm also a big believer in you have to,

00:04:16.969 --> 00:04:19.033
you play the cards that you're dealt.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:22.286
Like a good poker player
can win with any hand,

00:04:22.286 --> 00:04:24.524
so you just got to develop the skills,

00:04:24.524 --> 00:04:29.404
and a terrible poker player
can lose with two aces,

00:04:29.404 --> 00:04:32.945
and so just figuring out,
"This is what I've been dealt,"

00:04:32.945 --> 00:04:33.943
so what?

00:04:33.943 --> 00:04:35.586
Are you going to spend the entire
rest of your life complaining

00:04:35.586 --> 00:04:37.676
that you weren't born in the right country

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:40.135
or have the right parents
or have the right education

00:04:40.135 --> 00:04:41.985
or whatever excuses?

00:04:41.985 --> 00:04:44.342
You're just going to throw it in?

00:04:44.342 --> 00:04:46.140
That's your entire life now?

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.457
This is what you were dealt

00:04:47.457 --> 00:04:49.900
and so I'm going to spend the
rest of my life complaining?

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.041
You do what you can with what you have.

00:04:52.041 --> 00:04:53.677
That's one of my favorite quotes

00:04:53.677 --> 00:04:55.608
from Steve Wozniak, co-founder of Apple.

00:04:55.608 --> 00:04:57.609
They started with nothing.

00:04:57.609 --> 00:05:01.776
He sold his calculator to
raise money and to start Apple,

00:05:02.645 --> 00:05:04.618
and he loves saying that too many people

00:05:04.618 --> 00:05:06.464
focus on what they don't have,

00:05:06.464 --> 00:05:09.464
or the successful people think about

00:05:10.368 --> 00:05:14.933
what you should be doing with
what you already do have.

00:05:14.933 --> 00:05:16.903
You have a lot.

00:05:16.903 --> 00:05:19.591
You have brains, you have
the ability to hustle,

00:05:19.591 --> 00:05:24.128
you've got heart, you've got
ideas, you've got passion.

00:05:24.128 --> 00:05:26.494
You could turn that crazy
idea that's inside your head

00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:29.469
into reality, and you don't need luck,

00:05:29.469 --> 00:05:31.830
and you don't need most of the things

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.775
that people think you need.

00:05:33.775 --> 00:05:36.456
You just got to do the work every day

00:05:36.456 --> 00:05:38.647
and accept the responsibility that you are

00:05:38.647 --> 00:05:42.564
in your life where you
are only because of you.

00:05:44.145 --> 00:05:45.904
Once you take that responsibility

00:05:45.904 --> 00:05:48.381
and accountability, then you also realize

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.280
that you have the ability to change it.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.961
When you make that commitment,

00:05:52.961 --> 00:05:55.150
amazing things start to happen.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.960
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.130
what are your thoughts on luck?

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.888
Do you believe in it or not?

00:06:00.888 --> 00:06:02.844
Does it help you in your business?

00:06:02.844 --> 00:06:04.053
Do you need it?

00:06:04.053 --> 00:06:05.477
Is it a requirement for success?

00:06:05.477 --> 00:06:06.828
Let me know what you think.

00:06:06.828 --> 00:06:07.956
Leave it down in the comments.

00:06:07.956 --> 00:06:09.860
I'm really curious to find
out what you have to say.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.079
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Bonnie Ottaviani.

00:06:12.079 --> 00:06:14.657
Bonnie, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:06:14.657 --> 00:06:15.794
Your One Word.

00:06:15.794 --> 00:06:17.137
I really appreciate the support

00:06:17.137 --> 00:06:19.505
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:06:19.505 --> 00:06:20.504
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:20.504 --> 00:06:21.829
I believe in you.

00:06:21.829 --> 00:06:23.508
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:25.692
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:25.692 --> 00:06:27.783
Much love and I'll see
you guys tomorrow morning

00:06:27.783 --> 00:06:30.366
for another shot of entspresso.

00:06:31.451 --> 00:06:33.347
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:33.347 --> 00:06:36.930
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:42.042
- You know, people like Mozart

00:06:42.042 --> 00:06:44.935
and Beckham and the great athletes,

00:06:44.935 --> 00:06:48.514
humanitarians, entrepreneurs,
chess champions,

00:06:48.514 --> 00:06:52.097
were less about genetics
and natural talent

00:06:52.962 --> 00:06:57.129
and what makes icons in
whatever field you choose.

00:06:58.165 --> 00:07:00.086
It's not your talent.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:03.917
It's things like the
amount that you practice,

00:07:03.917 --> 00:07:06.341
your ability to stay with your practice

00:07:06.341 --> 00:07:09.736
for the 10,000 hours, your social circle.

00:07:09.736 --> 00:07:13.080
I mean, what made the great
Brazilian footballers great

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.201
was not that they have some natural thing

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:16.868
by living in Brazil.

00:07:18.448 --> 00:07:20.330
It's every little kid from pretty much

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.308
the moment he's three or
four years old, right,

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:25.304
sees the heroes and it's
the ticket out of poverty,

00:07:25.304 --> 00:07:27.378
and so all they do is touch the football

00:07:27.378 --> 00:07:29.222
every single day and night,

00:07:29.222 --> 00:07:31.293
and by the time they're 11 years old,

00:07:31.293 --> 00:07:33.425
they've touched the
football millions of times

00:07:33.425 --> 00:07:35.200
and they are therefore untouchable

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.258
compared to anyone else around the world,

00:07:37.258 --> 00:07:38.266
and all I'm saying is,

00:07:38.266 --> 00:07:40.091
genius is not something you're born with.

00:07:40.091 --> 00:07:41.724
Genius is something that you apply.

00:07:41.724 --> 00:07:44.583
You don't get lucky, you make lucky.

00:07:44.583 --> 00:07:47.102
Success is not something
that is, you know,

00:07:47.102 --> 00:07:48.918
divinely bestowed on you.

00:07:48.918 --> 00:07:52.597
Success, whether it's
prosperity or whatever it is,

00:07:52.597 --> 00:07:55.580
is something that you
earn by grit, hard work,

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.024
finding the right people,
doing the learning, et cetera.

00:07:59.024 --> 00:08:01.146
- Nothing in life is free.

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:03.575
Nothing happens overnight.

00:08:03.575 --> 00:08:06.150
It all takes tons and tons of work

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.092
and tons and tons of talent

00:08:08.092 --> 00:08:10.337
and tons of tons of serendipity,

00:08:10.337 --> 00:08:12.631
but my friends, luck, serendipity,

00:08:12.631 --> 00:08:14.326
there's a forced culture within that.

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:17.314
You know, you don't just
sit in your room hoping

00:08:17.314 --> 00:08:19.019
and then something lucky happens.

00:08:19.019 --> 00:08:20.961
Nobody just knocks on your
house's door and says,

00:08:20.961 --> 00:08:23.836
"Congratulations, you've
been awarded this."

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:27.169
Luck comes from being in the right spot.

00:08:30.104 --> 00:08:32.667
I've been really lucky
because I bleed out of my eyes

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:35.146
every day of my life and work my face off.

00:08:35.146 --> 00:08:39.805
You get really lucky when you
have that 11:30 PM meeting

00:08:39.805 --> 00:08:41.882
and one of the lucky thing happen.

00:08:41.882 --> 00:08:44.410
Pretty cool, since all you were sleeping.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.654
I was pretty lucky.

00:08:45.654 --> 00:08:48.084
Weird that I scheduled that meeting

00:08:48.084 --> 00:08:49.448
'cause I did a ton of things for 30 years

00:08:49.448 --> 00:08:51.108
that allowed me to even have
that meeting in the first place

00:08:51.108 --> 00:08:55.501
that gave me the leverage to
have that lucky thing happen.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.299
There's no overnight successes, period.

00:08:57.299 --> 00:08:58.294
They don't exist.

00:08:58.294 --> 00:09:00.444
Show me, leave a comment
on YouTube, leave the name,

00:09:00.444 --> 00:09:03.291
explain to me, tell me, show me,

00:09:03.291 --> 00:09:06.619
let me know, show me
the overnight success,

00:09:06.619 --> 00:09:09.722
because I'll show you you
justifying in your brain

00:09:09.722 --> 00:09:13.055
something that is just not true, period.

00:09:14.728 --> 00:09:17.817
- The universe of passion
is open to everybody.

00:09:17.817 --> 00:09:20.067
But many people don't know.

00:09:22.093 --> 00:09:26.973
They believe passion should
come down from the sky.

00:09:26.973 --> 00:09:29.640
No, you go to find your passion.

00:09:31.134 --> 00:09:32.999
Passion will not come to you.

00:09:32.999 --> 00:09:36.416
It is like luck, luck cannot come to you.

00:09:37.689 --> 00:09:39.518
You can buy as many Lotto things,

00:09:39.518 --> 00:09:43.635
you can make bets on Barcelona and Madrid.

00:09:43.635 --> 00:09:46.083
Luck will never come to you.

00:09:46.083 --> 00:09:49.750
But you go to luck,
that's much more secure.

00:09:51.022 --> 00:09:53.272
You go and go to take luck.

00:09:54.201 --> 00:09:57.981
If you stay and luck comes
down to you, forget it.

00:09:57.981 --> 00:10:00.696
You will die and no luck will ever come.

00:10:00.696 --> 00:10:04.863
Luck is a process where you
move to luck and you take luck

00:10:06.466 --> 00:10:09.744
and you say, "Come on
luck, I keep you now,"

00:10:09.744 --> 00:10:13.049
and you take another
one tomorrow and so on.

